-- title:
--   Orders at both branches of a monomial germ wV^e
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ that is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver L F` (every nonzero element has a principal divisor of degree zero, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$). Let $R_1,R_2$ be regular prolongations of $A$ to $F$ with residue fields $\bar F_1,\bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$ — each given by a valuation subring of $F$ lying over $A$ together with a surjective residue map onto $\bar F_i$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ can be rescaled by a constant into the ring with nonzero residue — and let $x_1,x_2$ be places of $\bar F_1,\bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$, with their order functions $\operatorname{ord}_{x_i}$. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/L$, all rational; let $\mathcal N_0\subseteq F$ be a local Noetherian subring contained in the integers of both $R_1$ and $R_2$, such that a place $P$ lies in $S$ exactly when $\mathcal N_0$ lies in its valuation subring and every non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$ has $P$-value in $A$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$, and such that every $f\in F$ has a nonzero $b\in\mathcal N_0$ with $fb$ an $L$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_0$. Let $C\subseteq L$ be a subring contained in $A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0$, a domain and discrete valuation ring, with $\varpi\in C$ nonzero such that an element of $C$ has zero residue in $A$ exactly when it is divisible by $\varpi$ in $C$; assume every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C$, that a $C$-linearly independent family of coefficients $c_i\in L$ can annihilate $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ with $a_i\in\mathcal N_0$ only if all $a_i=0$, that for $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq0$ some power $a^n$ is divisible by $b$, and that every $g\in\mathcal N_0$ becomes a non-unit after subtracting a suitable element of $C$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with $\pi\in W$ irreducible, $\sigma\colon W\to\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ a ring homomorphism into the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0$ at its maximal ideal sending $\pi$ to (the image of) $\varpi$, let $E\geq1$, and let $\iota\colon\widehat{\mathcal N_0}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ be a ring isomorphism carrying $\sigma$ to the constants `const`. Assume the two residue laws: for $f\in\mathcal N_0$ and $n\in\mathbb N$, if $R_1$-residue of $f$ is nonzero of order $n$ at $x_1$ then $\iota(f)$ is congruent to a unit times $V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by $\pi$ and $U$, and symmetrically with $R_2$, $x_2$, $U^n$ and the ideal generated by $\pi$ and $V$. Assume further the node coordinates $x,y\in\mathcal N_0$ with $R_1$-residue of $x$ zero, $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}$ of the $R_2$-residue of $x$ equal to $1$, $R_2$-residue of $y$ zero and $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}$ of the $R_1$-residue of $y$ equal to $1$. Then, for $a\in\mathcal N_0$, $e\geq1$ and a unit $w$ of the crossing model with $\iota(a)=w\,V^e$: the $R_2$-residue of $a$ vanishes; the $R_1$-residue of $a$ is nonzero with $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}=e$; and for every $c\in L$ with $c\cdot a$ in the integers of $R_2$ and nonzero $R_2$-residue, that residue has $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}=-e$.
--
--   This is the order law at a node presented by a crossing model: a germ which is a unit times the $e$-th power of one coordinate has a zero of order $e$ at the branch point of the first prolongation and, after any rescaling by a constant making it visible at the second end, a pole of order $e$ there. It is used in the construction of node presentations and node charts for modular curves at full level, where it is applied to the Hasse/Igusa-side coordinate $J-a_0$ with $R_1$ the Igusa-side end and $R_2$ the supersingular prolongation.
